KZ3 patch 4029 (network pass 50): pad_prompt_set_pad(), the glyph set of the pad that is plugged in even while the keys
were the last input (pad_prompt_set() answers keycaps then). The text layer (port/net/kz3_text_overrides.h,
kz3_net_hooks.h) names pad buttons in the game's own strings ("Swap L1 and L2", "Hold down R2") by this set:
Xbox pad LB/LT/RB/RT, PlayStation pad unchanged. No pad connected = the PS3 set (the game's text).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.19.0 (SPU pass 153): hunks unchanged; offsets and context follow the v0.19.0 chain (group A r152 files, Toro v019-c, R&C v019-b where delivered; originals for the rest, three-way merged where they did not apply).

diff --git a/libs/input/cellPad.c b/libs/input/cellPad.c
index 2c0d948..db486e9 100644
--- a/libs/input/cellPad.c
+++ b/libs/input/cellPad.c
@@ -1481,6 +1481,18 @@ int pad_prompt_set(void)
     return pad_prompt_set_for_device(dev);
 }
 
+/* KZ3 patch 4029 (network pass 50): the glyph set of the PAD that is plugged in, for text that names pad buttons
+ * (port/net/kz3_text_overrides.h kz3_tx_buttons: "Swap L1 and L2" -> "Swap LB and LT" on an Xbox pad). Same as
+ * pad_prompt_set(), except that keycaps (PAD_PROMPT_KBM, chosen or Auto) give the connected host pad's set, since a pad
+ * option row is about the pad even while the keys were the last input. No pad connected -> PS3 (the game's own text). */
+int pad_prompt_set_pad(void)
+{
+    int s = pad_prompt_set();
+    if (s != PAD_PROMPT_KBM) return s;
+    PadLastDevice none = { PAD_DEV_NONE, -1 };
+    return pad_prompt_set_for_device(pad_last_device_current(&none, s_host_state, s_port_dev, PAD_MAX_HOST_PORTS, NULL));
+}
+
 #ifdef _WIN32
 /* For 2039's keycap prompts: 1 when the prompts are keycaps (pad_prompt_set; was "the last input was a key"). */
 int pad_kb_last_device_keyboard(void)
